From 60e4a42c7786909e6a68d2de871f363c3605ca58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Tada Antunes <leotada523@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:29:34 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] gcbarrier: the GC write barrier as a GCC plugin for GDC

A GIMPLE pass, run before the lowering passes, that marks the 512-byte card of every
store of a pointer into memory that is not a variable or a global: inline
range-checked card store with release ordering, or a call to __sd_gc_card_range for
copies over 512 bytes or of unknown size. Defines version (D_GCBarrier) through the
frontend's exported function (gdc reserves D_* for -fversion). Same card ABI as LDC's
-gc-card-marking and DMD's -preview=gcbarrier.

With GCC 15.3.0 built from source, Linux x86-64: codegen_check.sh passes, and the
correctness battery passes with the instrumented libgphobos (mark_race: 0 violations
with the plugin, 17,936 without).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
